// Independent recipes: existing chains are inherited, not replaced wholesale.
// needs uses last week's supply; demand is an abstract input bill, not a stoichiometric balance.
// The bills are scaled so the world makes a little more of each than it asks for at the 2024
// start (SimBench "the world makes what the world needs"): phosphates were asked for at four
// times what the mines give, which put every country on Earth short of them for good.
{
  "copper_chain": {
    "good": "Copper", "output": { "deposit:Copper*extraction_efficiency": 1.0 },
    "demand": { "ElectronicsPlant": 0.238, "CivilianIndustry": 0.074, "ArmsIndustry": 0.089, "PowerPlant": 0.089 }
  },
